    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n87679" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προκατά-ληψις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>seizing in advance,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν ἐκβολῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Jul.
					<u>Or.</u>
					2.74c
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>preoccupation, anticipation</i> of an adversary's arguments,
				<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Rh.Al.</u>
				1428a8
			</span></i> (pl.), <i><span class="en">
				1432b11
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ -λήψει θέας</span> in
				<i>anticipation</i> of . . , <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>AJ</u>
				19.1.13
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>previous apprehension,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ π.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hsch.
				</span></i>
			
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καταφθατουμένη.</span>
			
		</div>
